+## Proposed foundational completion criteria for the public launch
+
+Owner planning direction,2026-10-15: there is no deadline-driven5.0 release.
+Complete most or all foundational verification, reproducibility, interoperability
+and provenance work before asking for coordinated-launch authorization. RFC0085–87
+and Issues354–355 are proposed launch components, not automatically deferred.
+The owner has **not accepted their tentative contracts** or authorized5.0 release
+preparation/publication. This section is the dependency-ordered proposal in the
+existing roadmap, not a separate planning system or package-version matrix.
+
+### Reconciled evidence and actual gaps
+
+Current main is `a18ed8ee` (#349 owner-approved DCF display correction), following
+merged documentation-only #353 (`66a354f`). Main CI38831554581 passes14 ordinary
+jobs,4,179 tests,1,089 reference checks and350 portable cases. The portable cases
+are Reader17, Verifier281, Integrity14, module1 and starter37. Issue354's older
+1,069/336 counts are a historical checkpoint. There is one implementation:
+`runner.py` invokes the TypeScript CLI; it is not an independent Python verifier.
+The dictionary currently has171 class calculation entries/89 distinct ids and11
+size-intensive entries; none constitutes the proposed L1 acquisition profile.
+
+Published4.3.0 remains the exact80c68c3d generation, Format3.0/Protocol4.1.0,
+verifier0.2.1. The later DCF correction is merged development, not retroactively
+published4.3.0 behavior. Phase1/Phase2 financial reports remain the evidence;
+local full-suite failures (including current3999pass/180fail) are not passing
+local gates. No independent Microsoft Excel recalculation has been established.
+
