+
+### Dependency order
+
+1. **Freeze evidence, not development.** Keep existing audit dispositions and
+   baseline source SHAs. Distinguish author-approved direction from accepted RFC,
+   implementation, conformance and publication. No5.0 package/version/tag work.
+2. **Resolve three design lanes in parallel:** RFC0085's history/projection
+   contract; RFC0086/87's separate comparison bases; draft0088's L1 procedures.
+   Base Python Reader/Verifier can proceed against the current contract now.
+3. **Accept bounded contracts before coding them.** Complete actual algorithms,
+   closed representations/conventions, error/applicability states and compatibility
+   paths. Issue355's convention comment is a proposal, not the registry. Do not
+   edit implemented RFC0078 or normative formulas on the strength of issue text.
+4. **Implement approved reference behavior with synthetic regression controls,**
+   keeping unrelated fixes bounded. Make newly required procedure/relationship
+   cases portable. Reuse the metric dictionary; do not create a second registry.
+5. **Complete independent Python base → L1 evidence** against the same accepted
+   corpus. Resolve spec gaps openly. Reuse deterministic definitions, not TS
+   source code/behavior as a hidden oracle; disclose provenance and permitted
+   shared normative data. Independent implementation does not mean using a
+   different algorithm where the standard pins one.
+6. **Converge cross-package, independent and spreadsheet evidence.** Test end-to-end
+   cash-flow identities, negative verdicts and unsupported conditions. Archive
+   signed/source-identity and projection scope evidence. New crypto dependencies
+   or signing claims require explicit capability decisions.
+7. **Only then request a launch decision.** Publish the evidence/limitations and
+   genuine outstanding exceptions in existing review/RFC/roadmap artifacts. Owner
+   approval of completion criteria is not approval of RFC semantics or permission
+   to prepare/tag/publish/deploy5.0.
+
+### Bounded scope and exclusions
+
+Recommend L1's first financial scope be stabilized multifamily, all equity or one
+fixed-rate loan, with explicitly declared inputs and complete equity/exit returns.
+The owner must confirm this boundary in draft0088. No automatic requirement for
+all possible asset classes, preferred-equity/multi-tranche forecast generation,
+lease rollover/recoveries, construction draws/tax, L2/L3 custom vectors, lender
+programs or general goal-seek. Existing builtin class/financing contracts remain
+valid and their existing claimed capabilities must keep passing.
+
+Require Python base Reader/Verifier **and L1** for the proposed foundational
+claim. Do not automatically require its module, portfolio, stochastic,
+sensitivity, full cryptographic Integrity or every representation profile.
+Python must not claim a profile on the strength of explicit unavailable outcomes.
+For the foundational provenance guarantee, require independently checked wrapper
+refusal, canonical/hash identity and continuity vectors; decide whether complete
+cross-implementation signed-archive verification is an advertised launch claim.
+If it is, an independent supported crypto verification path becomes a concrete
+prerequisite; a stdlib-only runtime's unchecked signatures are insufficient.
+
+RFC0086/87 can finish with a bounded accepted same-basis comparison contract and
+explicit unsupported-basis behavior; every external institutional accounting
+bridge is not required. Retaining distinct metrics must be a conscious accepted
+semantic choice with truthful claims, not an automatic deferral of reconciliation.
+Resolve provenance's unsafe legacy emission/retirement plan for launch rather
+than merely adding a marker older readers ignore. Actual breaking activation
+requires owner authorization and honest semver; interim4.x development continues
+through additive APIs, accepted compatible fixes and draft design work.
+
+### Evidence that will actually close a launch criterion
+
+A workstream closes only with an accepted contract where needed, its implemented
+behavior, passing applicable positive/negative conformance, independently scoped
+evidence and known limitations. A proposal, issue closure, a receipt over stated
+inputs, reference+portable-driver success, emitted XLSX, or equal cached values
+alone cannot close the corresponding foundational guarantee. Quantify tested
+coverage and explain omissions; do not advertise universal economic correctness.
+Record the exact supported runtime/OS matrix rather than assuming every Python
+profile or platform is certified. There is no foundation-completion claim yet.
+
+Owner decisions still needed: approve/amend this bounded launch scope; D1–D5 of
+draft0085; RFC0086/87 authority/basis/precision/applicability; draft0088 procedures
+and packaging; Python location/runtime/dependency/distribution (PyPI setup needs
+separate authorization); actual spreadsheet engine/access and parity scope;
+required signed-history independence scope; and eventual coordinated versioning.
+The owner can change the proposed gates explicitly, with the resulting guarantee
+and evidence limitation stated. No calendar deadline overrides a correctness gap.
+
